            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0080" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg34"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.751/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Governor of New York</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Whitman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 28, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Governor</hi>: I am in receipt of your
                    letter of the 24th in which you advise me that the measure concerning which I
                    wrote you on the 19th was vetoed by you. I believe your action will save the
                    Federal Government very serious embarrassment and I heartily thank you for the
                    prompt and wise course which you have taken in regard to the proposed
                    legislation.</p>
                <p>With warm regards [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
